insert into kb_review_queue (target, proposed_fact, raw_input, reason, conflicting_with, submitted_by)
select $q$common$q$, $q$Without Future Engraving, a charm or engraving is added by a discounted reorder: MYKA and theo grace non-premium 70% off, premium 50% off, Oak & Luna 50% and 30%. Coupons of 30% (MYKA) or 20% (Oak & Luna) apply when the item is archived or the maximum is reached.$q$, $q$[Adding an engraving or charm after purchase, discounts and the three special products] Future Engraving document: without Future Engraving, a reorder at a discount (MYKA non-premium 70% off, premium 50%, Oak & Luna 50% and 30%), process written as 'for 50% of the price for non-premium or 30% for premium', and 30% (MYKA) or 20% (Oak & Luna) coupons for archived items or a maximum reached. Earlier instruction for Russian Rings, Heritage Multiple Name and Totem 3D Bar: no partial addition, full repurchase with GRACE30 (30% off). Macros: a unique 20% code, or 30% with team lead approval. Add-on warranty pack macros: $40 for gold and diamond items.$q$, $q$The discounts are written two ways in the same document (70% and 50% for MYKA, but '50% of the price' and '30%' in the process, which are the Oak & Luna figures). It is also unclear whether the three products that previously only allowed a full repurchase with GRACE30 can use the discounted reorder, and whether the add-on warranty pack is the same thing as Future Engraving.$q$, $q$Theo grace Future Engraving facts and the Presale adding a bead or charm rule.$q$, 'source reconciliation'
